  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Security: the .NET 10 servicing packages move to 10.0.15, fixing GHSA-x33c-w48q-qrgc (CVE-2026-114149, an ASP.NET Core denial of service) in Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities. PDFileExplorer: NavigateToFolderAsync opens a folder itself, loading its contents once without first showing the folder holding it; it returns false, with the deepest folder found open, when the folder is not there. A hidden preview panel no longer fetches a preview for every selection: PDFilePreview gains IsVisible, and the item chosen while it was hidden is fetched once it shows. PDContextMenu now opens at the pointer under CSS zoom or a scaled parent, and is no longer clipped by a panel that scrolls, using popper 2's fixed placement in place of popper 1's option, which popper 2 ignored. It sits above sticky headers at a z-index of 1000, which --pd-contextmenu-z-index overrides. Given an ExceptionHandler, PDContextMenu passes a failure in showing the menu or in an item's click to it instead of ending the Blazor circuit; without one, a failure is thrown as before, and PDFileExplorer passes its own handler to its menus.",
